                <pb facs="0216" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4 A 2/121b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-10-25T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>84. American Delegation to Opium Conference at Geneva will consist of Honorable
                    Stephen G. Porter, chairman, Eight Reverend Charles H. Brent, Assistant Surgeon
                    General Rupert Blue, Mrs. Hamilton Wright, Mr. Edwin L. Neville, delegates, with
                    five assistants and clerks. Please notify Secretary General of League of Nations
                    and the appropriate Swiss authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
